{
 "_doc": "Tier-3 wilderness set piece for random worlds (site forest). A two-storey log hunting lodge: the kit rooms wear the w3_lodge_shell (chinked bark-on logs saddle-notched at the corners, cut for every door and window: its catalog entry mirrors this plan's lodge rectangle, cols 4..19, rows 4..13) under a cedar gable roof, with a fieldstone chimney stack outside the great room's west wall and the fireplace inside it. The plan ends at the lodge's front so the porch runs along it; the yard in front (the track, the truck, the sign) lies outside the plan. A double-height great room (storeys 2) with the trophy wall, the antler chandelier and a balcony (a rail gallery) over it; kitchen, hall and stairs, the gun room and the boot room; guest rooms and the guide's room upstairs; a cellar (root cellar and meat locker) under the kitchen, cut into the terrain; outside, the skinning shed and two kennel runs. Route: the track -> the porch, its doors piled shut -> round past the kennels -> a kitchen window smashed in behind (jaws under it: their snap wakes the hunters) -> the kitchen, Marit's note -> down to the cellar -> the meat locker: Arne's keys (taking them wakes the locker) -> back up through the great room: the hunters round the hearth rise -> the hall -> the gun room's deadbolt, a shotgun wired behind it -> Marit (guardian) and the guns -> unbolt the gun room's door to the yard. Upstairs is optional: the sick guests, a balcony whose boards have rotted. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
